============================================================
4. COUNT EMPLOYEES PER DEPARTMENT
============================================================

Input

DeptId | Employee
-------+---------
10     | John
10     | Mary
20     | Steve
20     | Tom
30     | David

Query

SELECT DeptId,
       COUNT(*) AS EmpCount
FROM Employee
GROUP BY DeptId;

Output

DeptId | EmpCount
-------+---------
10     | 2
20     | 2
30     | 1

Explanation

GROUP BY creates one group for each DeptId.
COUNT(*) counts the rows in each department group.

============================================================
5. DEPARTMENTS HAVING MORE THAN ONE EMPLOYEE
============================================================

Input

DeptId | Employees
-------+------------
10     | John, Mary
20     | Steve, Tom
30     | David

Query

SELECT DeptId,
       COUNT(*) AS EmpCount
FROM Employee
GROUP BY DeptId
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

Output

DeptId | EmpCount
-------+---------
10     | 2
20     | 2

Explanation

GROUP BY creates department groups.
HAVING filters the groups after COUNT(*) is calculated.
Department 30 is excluded because it has only one employee.

