6. INNER JOIN EXAMPLE
============================================================

Input

Employee

Name  | DeptId
------+-------
John  | 10
Mary  | 10
Steve | 20
Tom   | 20
David | 30

Department

DeptId | DeptName
-------+---------
10     | IT
20     | HR
30     | Finance

Query

SELECT e.Name,
       d.DeptName
FROM Employee e
INNER JOIN Department d
    ON e.DeptId = d.DeptId;

Output

Name  | DeptName
------+---------
John  | IT
Mary  | IT
Steve | HR
Tom   | HR
David | Finance

Explanation

INNER JOIN returns rows having matching DeptId values in both tables.
Employee names are combined with their corresponding department names.

