============================================================
12. FIND THE THIRD-HIGHEST SALARY USING ROW_NUMBER
============================================================

Input

Name  | Salary
------+-------
John  | 50000
Mary  | 70000
Steve | 60000
Tom   | 80000
David | 90000

Query

WITH X AS
(
    SELECT Salary,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY Salary DESC) AS rn
    FROM Employee
)
SELECT Salary
FROM X
WHERE rn = 3;

Output

Salary
------
70000

Explanation

ROW_NUMBER assigns a unique sequence after sorting salaries descending.

90000 -> 1
80000 -> 2
70000 -> 3
60000 -> 4
50000 -> 5

The row numbered 3 contains salary 70000.
Note: With duplicate salaries, this finds the third row, not necessarily the
third-highest distinct salary.

